//@version=6
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// © Market_Logic_India                                                                    MPL-2.0
// BEHAVIOURAL PRESSURE MAP                                                                    v1.2
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// OVERVIEW
//   A map of where the market's HOLDERS sit, and what behavioural finance says they will do there.
//   Every past bar is a cohort that bought around its price on its volume; each cohort's UNREALISED
//   profit/loss is run through the Kahneman-Tversky prospect-theory value function, and the
//   disposition effect (sell winners, hold losers) turns that into real supply and demand:
//     • Trapped LOSERS above price wait to get back to break-even → BEHAVIOURAL RESISTANCE
//       (loss-aversion λ makes it sticky).
//     • In-profit cohorts below price mark high-volume DEMAND nodes the market defends → SUPPORT.
//     • The recency-weighted average cost is a reference-point MAGNET price gravitates toward.
//   The pane plots the NET behavioural pressure (−100 heavy overhead supply … +100 clean, in-profit
//   float); the price chart is annotated with the strongest support / resistance cost-basis nodes
//   and the magnet. It is a map of positioning pressure, not a buy/sell signal.
//
// WHAT MAKES IT DIFFERENT
//   Volume profiles show WHERE volume traded. This adds WHY it matters: it weights each price level
//   by the unrealised P&L of the people who own it and by how loss-aversion and the disposition
//   effect make them act. A level with heavy TRAPPED-LONG volume above is stronger resistance than a
//   same-size node of comfortable winners — prospect theory, not raw volume, sizes the pressure.
//
// HOW IT WORKS
//   1. Over a lookback, each bar is a cohort: cost basis ≈ HLC3, size = volume × recency-decay.
//   2. Cohort unrealised return g = (price − cost)/cost → value v(g) = g^α (gain) or −λ·(−g)^β (loss).
//   3. Demand (profit nodes below) and loss-averse supply (trapped above) are summed; the oscillator
//      is their balance, 100·(Demand − Supply)/(Demand + Supply).
//   4. The cohorts are binned to find the strongest support/resistance nodes and the % of float in
//      profit; a forward calibration harness checks whether node rejections actually paid.
//
// HOW TO USE
//   Read the pane for pressure (green/above 0 = supportive, in-profit float; red/below 0 = overhead
//   supply). On price, red lines are behavioural resistance (trapped longs), green lines support
//   (defended profit nodes), the yellow line is the magnet. Triangles mark a node rejection with
//   supportive pressure. % in profit is a sentiment gauge — very high can mean euphoria/distribution
//   risk, very low can mean capitulation. Context, never a standalone trigger.
//
// UNIVERSAL / SOURCES
//   Lookback, recency half-life, bin count and the prospect-theory parameters are all inputs. Needs
//   volume; works on any symbol/timeframe. Defaults suit liquid index/futures behaviour — widen the
//   lookback or shorten the half-life to retune for slower or faster instruments.
//
// CONCEPT CREDIT
//   Prospect theory & the value function — Daniel Kahneman & Amos Tversky (1979). Disposition effect
//   — Hersh Shefrin & Meir Statman (1985); Terrance Odean (1998). Reference-point / cost-basis
//   dynamics — Grinblatt & Han (2005). Sample-uniqueness weighting & out-of-sample evaluation —
//   Marcos López de Prado (2018). Original implementation; not affiliated with any third party.
//
// HONESTY / LIMITATIONS
//   Cost basis is APPROXIMATED by each bar's HLC3 and volume — it is not real holder data. The value
//   function is a model of behaviour, not a law. The pressure and nodes are descriptive positioning
//   context; the Edge row (in-sample and out-of-sample) is what tells you if node rejections have
//   paid on THIS symbol. Nothing here predicts price.
//
// DISCLAIMER
//   Research and educational tool only. NOT financial advice and NO guarantee of profitability or
//   accuracy. Trading carries risk of loss. Test out-of-sample and make your own decisions.
//
// Non-repaint: cohorts use closed bars; the calibration resolves on confirmed bars only.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
indicator("Behavioural Pressure Map", "BehavPress", overlay = false, max_bars_back = 600, max_lines_count = 100, max_labels_count = 60)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                                          INPUTS
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
g1 = "01 · Data & window"
lookN   = input.int(240, "Cohort lookback (bars)", minval = 30, maxval = 500, group = g1, tooltip = "How many past bars are treated as holder cohorts. Longer = more of the float, heavier compute.")
recHL   = input.float(120.0, "Recency half-life (bars)", minval = 5.0, maxval = 1000.0, step = 5.0, group = g1, tooltip = "Older cohorts decay: a cohort this many bars back counts half as much as today's. Smaller = only the recent float matters.")
nBins   = input.int(50, "Price bins (nodes)", minval = 10, maxval = 100, group = g1, tooltip = "Resolution of the cost-basis distribution used to locate support / resistance nodes.")

g2 = "02 · Prospect theory"
alphaG  = input.float(0.88, "Value curvature α (gains)", minval = 0.3, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.01, group = g2, tooltip = "Kahneman-Tversky diminishing sensitivity to gains. 0.88 = original estimate.")
betaG   = input.float(0.88, "Value curvature β (losses)", minval = 0.3, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.01, group = g2)
lamL    = input.float(2.25, "Loss aversion λ", minval = 1.0, maxval = 4.0, step = 0.05, group = g2, tooltip = "How much more a loss weighs than an equal gain. 2.25 = original estimate; higher = stickier break-even resistance.")

g3 = "03 · Nodes & signals"
maxNodes= input.int(6, "Max nodes drawn per side", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = g3)
nodeFrac= input.float(0.35, "Node strength threshold (× peak)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.9, step = 0.05, group = g3, tooltip = "Draw a level only if its cohort weight is at least this fraction of the strongest node.")
pThr    = input.float(20.0, "Pressure threshold", minval = 0.0, maxval = 90.0, step = 5.0, group = g3, tooltip = "Net pressure beyond ± this is a decisive supply/demand imbalance (tints, gates signals).")
proxATR = input.float(0.5, "Node proximity (× ATR)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.1, group = g3, tooltip = "How close price must tag a node to count as a rejection.")
sigGap  = input.int(10, "Min bars between signals", minval = 1, maxval = 200, group = g3)
showSig = input.bool(true, "Mark node-rejection signals", group = g3)
confirmSig = input.bool(true, "Non-repaint: confirm signals on bar close", group = g3, tooltip = "ON (default): a node-rejection signal, its alert and its marker are settled on the CLOSED bar, so what you see matches what the Edge harness measures and nothing repaints intrabar. OFF: signals form live on the current bar (they may flicker until close).")

g4 = "04 · Calibration harness"
calcCal = input.bool(true, "Measure Edge", group = g4, tooltip = "Log each node-rejection signal and, a horizon later, check whether price moved ≥ k×ATR the signalled way vs a random bar.")
calHor  = input.int(10, "Forward horizon (bars)", minval = 2, maxval = 100, group = g4)
calMove = input.float(0.8, "Move threshold (× ATR)", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = g4)
atrLen  = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 1, group = g4)
trainN  = input.int(30, "In-sample events (then OOS)", minval = 10, group = g4, tooltip = "First N resolved events train; later ones are scored out-of-sample. The OOS edge is the trustworthy one.")
nTests  = input.int(3, "Edge significance · N tests (deflation)", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = g4)

g5 = "05 · Regime (optional)"
useRegime = input.bool(false, "Consume external regime (EXP_Regime)", group = g5, tooltip = "Link to the Market Regime Classifier's EXP_Regime (−2…+2); support bounces need regime ≥ 0, resistance rejections need ≤ 0.")
regSrc    = input.source(close, "Regime source (link to EXP_Regime)", group = g5)

g6 = "06 · Visual & theme"
visStyle = input.string("Gradient area + glow", "Oscillator style", options = ["Gradient area + glow","Histogram","Line"], group = g6)
showNodes= input.bool(true, "Draw cost-basis nodes on price", group = g6)
showMag  = input.bool(true, "Draw break-even magnet on price", group = g6)
showTint = input.bool(true, "Background pressure tint", group = g6)
showDash = input.bool(true, "Show dashboard", group = g6)
dashMode = input.string("Compact", "Dashboard detail", options = ["Compact","Pro"], group = g6, tooltip = "Compact = verdict, pressure, % in profit, the two nearest cost-basis nodes and the out-of-sample edge. Pro = the full calibration + magnet + eff-N breakdown.")
dashPos  = input.string("Top Right", "Dashboard position", options = ["Top Right","Top Left","Bottom Right","Bottom Left","Middle Right"], group = g6)
themeOpt = input.string("Auto (match chart)", "Theme", options = ["Auto (match chart)","Dark","Light"], group = g6)
colSup   = input.color(#2ebd85, "Support / in-profit", group = g6)
colRes   = input.color(#f6465d, "Resistance / overhang", group = g6)
colMagI  = input.color(#f7c948, "Magnet / midline", group = g6)

gZ = "Z · Identity & exports"
showId  = input.bool(true, "Show identity strip", group = gZ)
showEXP = input.bool(true, "Emit EXP_* exports", group = gZ)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                                       THEME / HELPERS
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_lum(color cc) => na(cc) ? 0.0 : 0.299 * color.r(cc) + 0.587 * color.g(cc) + 0.114 * color.b(cc)
bool  uiDark  = themeOpt == "Dark" ? true : themeOpt == "Light" ? false : f_lum(chart.bg_color) < 140
color panelBg = uiDark ? color.rgb(17, 22, 28)    : color.rgb(244, 246, 248)
color rowAlt  = uiDark ? color.rgb(25, 31, 39)    : color.rgb(232, 236, 240)
color txtMain = uiDark ? color.white              : color.rgb(16, 20, 24)
color txtSub  = uiDark ? color.rgb(154, 166, 178) : color.rgb(74, 82, 91)
color txtMut  = uiDark ? color.rgb(110, 120, 132) : color.rgb(140, 148, 156)
color frameC  = uiDark ? color.rgb(58, 70, 84)    : color.rgb(196, 204, 212)
color cSup    = uiDark ? colSup : color.rgb(14, 124, 90)
color cRes    = uiDark ? colRes : color.rgb(198, 40, 40)
f_txtOn(color cc) => f_lum(cc) > 140 ? color.rgb(10, 10, 10) : color.white
f_pos(string s) => s == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : s == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : s == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : s == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : position.top_right

float atr   = ta.atr(atrLen)
float decay = math.pow(0.5, 1.0 / recHL)                      // recency decay per bar
float pLo   = ta.lowest(low, lookN)
float pHi   = ta.highest(high, lookN)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                   ENGINE · cohort pressure + cost-basis binning (one pass)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
int   L = math.min(lookN, bar_index)
float P = close

var array<float> binVol = array.new<float>(nBins, 0.0)        // reused each bar (cleared below)
float binW = (pHi > pLo) ? (pHi - pLo) / nBins : na

float dem = 0.0                                               // demand below (in-profit nodes)
float sup = 0.0                                               // loss-averse supply overhang above
float sumW = 0.0
float magNum = 0.0
float profW = 0.0
if not na(binW) and binW > 0.0 and L > 5
    for b = 0 to nBins - 1
        array.set(binVol, b, 0.0)
    // Recency weight decays geometrically with age j. Carrying it forward as a
    // running product (decayPow *= decay) replaces one math.pow() per cohort per
    // bar with a single multiply — the largest per-bar saving in the engine, and
    // numerically identical to math.pow(decay, j).
    float decayPow = 1.0
    for j = 0 to L - 1
        float c = hlc3[j]
        float vv = nz(volume[j])
        float wj = vv * decayPow
        if wj > 0.0 and c > 0.0
            float g = (P - c) / c
            sumW += wj
            magNum += wj * c
            if c < P
                dem += wj * math.pow(math.abs(g), alphaG)
                profW += wj
            else if c > P
                sup += wj * lamL * math.pow(math.abs(g), betaG)
            int bi = math.max(0, math.min(nBins - 1, int((c - pLo) / binW)))
            array.set(binVol, bi, array.get(binVol, bi) + wj)
        decayPow *= decay

float netPressure = (dem + sup) > 0.0 ? 100.0 * (dem - sup) / (dem + sup) : na
float magnet      = sumW > 0.0 ? magNum / sumW : na
float pctProfit   = sumW > 0.0 ? 100.0 * profW / sumW : na

// strongest support node (below P) and resistance node (above P), plus the peak weight
float peakW = 0.0
if not na(binW)
    for b = 0 to nBins - 1
        peakW := math.max(peakW, array.get(binVol, b))
float nearSup = na
float supStr  = 0.0
float nearRes = na
float resStr  = 0.0
if not na(binW) and peakW > 0.0
    for b = 0 to nBins - 1
        float bc = pLo + (b + 0.5) * binW
        float bw = array.get(binVol, b)
        if bc < P and bw > supStr
            supStr := bw
            nearSup := bc
        if bc > P and bw > resStr
            resStr := bw
            nearRes := bc

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                                        SIGNALS
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
int  regId    = (useRegime and not na(regSrc) and math.abs(regSrc) <= 2.5) ? int(math.round(regSrc)) : na
bool regBull  = not useRegime or (not na(regId) and regId >= 0)
bool regBear  = not useRegime or (not na(regId) and regId <= 0)
bool atSup = not na(nearSup) and not na(atr) and low <= nearSup + proxATR * atr and close > nearSup
bool atRes = not na(nearRes) and not na(atr) and high >= nearRes - proxATR * atr and close < nearRes
var int lastSigBar = na
bool cooled = na(lastSigBar) or (bar_index - lastSigBar) >= sigGap
bool sigOK = (not confirmSig) or barstate.isconfirmed   // non-repaint gate: settle on close
bool bull = showSig and sigOK and atSup and not na(netPressure) and netPressure > pThr and regBull and cooled
bool bear = showSig and sigOK and atRes and not na(netPressure) and netPressure < -pThr and regBear and cooled
if bull or bear
    lastSigBar := bar_index

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                              CALIBRATION HARNESS (HARNESS+)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_wilson(float w, float n, float zc) =>
    float r = na
    if n > 0.0
        float pp = w / n
        float den = 1.0 + zc * zc / n
        r := zc * math.sqrt(pp * (1.0 - pp) / n + zc * zc / (4.0 * n * n)) / den
    r

var array<int>   cDir  = array.new<int>()
var array<int>   cBar  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> cEnt  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> cAtr  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> cUniq = array.new<float>()
var int   hits    = 0
var int   tot     = 0
var float hitsW   = 0.0
var float totW    = 0.0
var int   isHits  = 0
var int   isTot   = 0
var int   oosHits = 0
var int   oosTot  = 0
var int   resolvedC = 0
var int   baseTot = 0
var int   baseUp  = 0
var int   baseDn  = 0
float fwdMv  = close - close[calHor]
float fwdAtr = atr[calHor]

if calcCal and barstate.isconfirmed and not na(atr) and atr > 0.0
    if bull
        cDir.push(1),  cBar.push(bar_index), cEnt.push(close), cAtr.push(atr), cUniq.push(1.0 / (1.0 + cBar.size()))
    if bear
        cDir.push(-1), cBar.push(bar_index), cEnt.push(close), cAtr.push(atr), cUniq.push(1.0 / (1.0 + cBar.size()))
    if bar_index > calHor and not na(fwdAtr) and fwdAtr > 0.0
        baseTot += 1
        if fwdMv >= calMove * fwdAtr
            baseUp += 1
        if -fwdMv >= calMove * fwdAtr
            baseDn += 1
    if cBar.size() > 0
        for i = cBar.size() - 1 to 0
            if bar_index - cBar.get(i) >= calHor
                int   d = cDir.get(i)
                float fav = (close - cEnt.get(i)) * d
                bool  win = fav >= calMove * cAtr.get(i)
                float w = cUniq.get(i)
                tot += 1
                totW += w
                hits := win ? hits + 1 : hits
                hitsW := win ? hitsW + w : hitsW
                if resolvedC < trainN
                    isTot += 1
                    isHits := win ? isHits + 1 : isHits
                else
                    oosTot += 1
                    oosHits := win ? oosHits + 1 : oosHits
                resolvedC += 1
                cDir.remove(i), cBar.remove(i), cEnt.remove(i), cAtr.remove(i), cUniq.remove(i)

float baseP   = baseTot > 0 ? (baseUp + baseDn) * 100.0 / (2.0 * baseTot) : na
float hitP    = tot > 0 ? hits * 100.0 / tot : na
float edge    = (not na(hitP) and not na(baseP)) ? hitP - baseP : na
float zDefl   = nTests <= 1 ? 1.96 : nTests == 2 ? 2.24 : nTests == 3 ? 2.39 : nTests == 4 ? 2.50 : 2.58
float effN    = totW
float oosHitP = oosTot > 0 ? oosHits * 100.0 / oosTot : na
float oosEdge = (not na(oosHitP) and not na(baseP)) ? oosHitP - baseP : na
float oosCi   = f_wilson(oosHits, oosTot, zDefl) * 100.0
bool  oosStar = oosTot >= 10 and not na(oosHitP) and not na(baseP) and (oosHitP - oosCi) > baseP

// verdict
int vCode = na(netPressure) ? -1 : netPressure > pThr ? 2 : netPressure < -pThr ? 0 : 1
string vTxt = vCode == -1 ? "warming up…" : vCode == 2 ? "support base · clean overhead" : vCode == 0 ? "supply overhang · capped" : "balanced positioning"

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                                          PLOTS (pane)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
bool isArea = visStyle == "Gradient area + glow"
bool isHist = visStyle == "Histogram"
bool showGlow = not isHist
color oscCol = na(netPressure) ? color.gray : netPressure >= 0 ? cSup : cRes
float intensity = math.min(1.0, math.abs(nz(netPressure)) / 100.0)

bgcolor(showTint and not na(netPressure) and netPressure >= pThr ? color.new(cSup, 90) : showTint and not na(netPressure) and netPressure <= -pThr ? color.new(cRes, 90) : na, title = "Pressure tint")

plot(0.0, "Mid glow", color = color.new(colMagI, 80), linewidth = 6, display = display.pane)
hline(0, "Zero", color = color.new(colMagI, 0), linestyle = hline.style_solid)
plot(pThr,  "Demand band", color = color.new(cSup, 60), linewidth = 1, display = display.pane, editable = false)
plot(-pThr, "Supply band", color = color.new(cRes, 60), linewidth = 1, display = display.pane, editable = false)

// Glow brightens with pressure magnitude, so a decisive supply/demand imbalance
// visibly radiates while balanced positioning stays faint — the strength of the
// move reads at a glance from the halo, not just the line's height.
int glowOuterT = 82 - int(28 * intensity)
int glowInnerT = 55 - int(25 * intensity)
plot(showGlow ? netPressure : na, "glow outer", color = color.new(oscCol, glowOuterT), linewidth = 8, display = display.pane)
plot(showGlow ? netPressure : na, "glow inner", color = color.new(oscCol, glowInnerT), linewidth = 4, display = display.pane)
pMain = plot(showGlow ? netPressure : na, "Net pressure", color = oscCol, linewidth = 2, display = display.pane)
plot(isHist ? netPressure : na, "Histogram", color = color.new(oscCol, 20), style = plot.style_columns, display = display.pane)
pBase = plot(isArea ? 0.0 : na, "base", color = na, display = display.none, editable = false)
fill(pMain, pBase, color = isArea ? color.new(oscCol, 90 - int(45 * intensity)) : na, title = "Area")

// pane rejection marks + PRICE overlay triangles
plotshape(bull, "Support bounce", shape.triangleup,   location.bottom, color = cSup, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(bear, "Resistance reject", shape.triangledown, location.top,  color = cRes, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(bull, "Support bounce (overlay)",   shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color = cSup, size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true)
plotshape(bear, "Resistance reject (overlay)", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color = cRes, size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                       COST-BASIS NODES + MAGNET on price (last bar)
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var array<line> nodeLines = array.new<line>()
var line magLine = na
if barstate.islast and not na(binW) and peakW > 0.0
    if nodeLines.size() > 0
        for i = 0 to nodeLines.size() - 1
            line.delete(nodeLines.get(i))
    nodeLines.clear()
    if not na(magLine)
        line.delete(magLine)
    int drawnUp = 0
    int drawnDn = 0
    if showNodes
        for b = nBins - 1 to 0
            float bw = array.get(binVol, b)
            if bw >= nodeFrac * peakW
                float bc = pLo + (b + 0.5) * binW
                bool above = bc > P
                bool ok = above ? drawnUp < maxNodes : drawnDn < maxNodes
                if ok
                    color lc = above ? cRes : cSup
                    int tp = math.min(90, 40 + int(50.0 * (1.0 - bw / peakW)))
                    // Width also tracks node strength, so the heaviest cost-basis
                    // walls are the boldest lines, not just the least transparent.
                    float strRatio = bw / peakW
                    int nw = strRatio >= 0.66 ? 3 : strRatio >= 0.4 ? 2 : 1
                    line ln = line.new(bar_index - L, bc, bar_index, bc, color = color.new(lc, tp), width = nw, extend = extend.right, force_overlay = true)
                    nodeLines.push(ln)
                    if above
                        drawnUp += 1
                    else
                        drawnDn += 1
    if showMag and not na(magnet)
        magLine := line.new(bar_index - L, magnet, bar_index, magnet, color = color.new(colMagI, 20), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, extend = extend.right, force_overlay = true)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                                        DASHBOARD
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
int dRows = dashMode == "Pro" ? 11 : 6
var table dash = table.new(f_pos(dashPos), 2, dRows, frame_color = frameC, frame_width = 1, border_color = frameC, border_width = 1)
f_cell(int r, string k, string v, color vc, color bg) =>
    table.cell(dash, 0, r, k, text_color = txtSub, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left,  bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(dash, 1, r, v, text_color = vc,     text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right, bgcolor = bg)

if showDash and barstate.islast
    table.set_bgcolor(dash, panelBg)
    color vCol = vCode == 2 ? cSup : vCode == 0 ? cRes : txtMut
    color hdr  = color.new(vCode == 2 ? cSup : vCode == 0 ? cRes : color.gray, 0)
    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, dashMode == "Pro" ? "BEHAV PRESSURE" : "BEHAV PRESS", text_color = f_txtOn(hdr), bgcolor = hdr, text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, vTxt, text_color = f_txtOn(hdr), bgcolor = hdr, text_size = size.tiny)
    if dashMode == "Pro"
        f_cell(1, "Net pressure", na(netPressure) ? "-" : str.tostring(netPressure, "0"), vCol, rowAlt)
        f_cell(2, "% float in profit", na(pctProfit) ? "-" : str.tostring(pctProfit, "0") + "%", pctProfit > 80 ? cRes : pctProfit < 20 ? cSup : txtMain, panelBg)
        f_cell(3, "Magnet (break-even)", na(magnet) ? "-" : str.tostring(magnet, format.mintick), txtMain, rowAlt)
        f_cell(4, "Resistance node", na(nearRes) ? "-" : str.tostring(nearRes, format.mintick), cRes, panelBg)
        f_cell(5, "Support node", na(nearSup) ? "-" : str.tostring(nearSup, format.mintick), cSup, rowAlt)
        f_cell(6, "Signals (n)", str.tostring(tot), txtMain, panelBg)
        f_cell(7, "Hit % (edge)", na(hitP) ? "warming" : str.tostring(hitP, "0") + "%  " + (na(edge) ? "" : (edge >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(edge, "0.0")), na(edge) ? txtMut : edge > 0 ? cSup : cRes, rowAlt)
        f_cell(8, "Base %", na(baseP) ? "-" : str.tostring(baseP, "0") + "%", txtMut, panelBg)
        f_cell(9, "Edge (OOS)", na(oosEdge) ? "warming" : (oosStar ? "★ " : "") + (oosEdge >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(oosEdge, "0.0"), na(oosEdge) ? txtMut : oosEdge > 0 ? cSup : cRes, rowAlt)
        f_cell(10, "Eff-N (IS/OOS)", str.tostring(effN, "0.0") + " (" + str.tostring(isTot) + "/" + str.tostring(oosTot) + ")", txtMain, panelBg)
    else
        f_cell(1, "Net pressure", na(netPressure) ? "-" : str.tostring(netPressure, "0"), vCol, rowAlt)
        f_cell(2, "% float in profit", na(pctProfit) ? "-" : str.tostring(pctProfit, "0") + "%", pctProfit > 80 ? cRes : pctProfit < 20 ? cSup : txtMain, panelBg)
        f_cell(3, "Resistance node", na(nearRes) ? "-" : str.tostring(nearRes, format.mintick), cRes, rowAlt)
        f_cell(4, "Support node", na(nearSup) ? "-" : str.tostring(nearSup, format.mintick), cSup, panelBg)
        f_cell(5, "Edge (OOS)", na(oosEdge) ? "warming" : (oosStar ? "★ " : "") + (oosEdge >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(oosEdge, "0.0"), na(oosEdge) ? txtMut : oosEdge > 0 ? cSup : cRes, rowAlt)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                                    IDENTITY STRIP
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var table idT = table.new(position.bottom_center, 1, 1, force_overlay = true)
if showId and barstate.islast
    table.cell(idT, 0, 0, "Behavioural Pressure Map   -   " + syminfo.ticker + "   -   " + timeframe.period, text_color = uiDark ? color.new(#c8d0da, 10) : color.new(#2a2f37, 10), text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_center, bgcolor = color.new(color.gray, 100))

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//                                    ALERTS + EXPORTS
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
alertcondition(bull, "Support bounce", "Behavioural Pressure: price rejected a support cost-basis node with demand pressure.")
alertcondition(bear, "Resistance reject", "Behavioural Pressure: price rejected a resistance cost-basis node with supply pressure.")
alertcondition(ta.crossover(nz(netPressure), pThr)   and sigOK, "Demand takes over", "Behavioural Pressure: net pressure turned decisively supportive.")
alertcondition(ta.crossunder(nz(netPressure), -pThr) and sigOK, "Supply takes over", "Behavioural Pressure: net pressure turned decisively overhead-supply.")

color exC_ = color.new(color.gray, 100)
plot(showEXP ? netPressure : na, "EXP_Pressure",  color = exC_, display = display.data_window)
plot(showEXP ? magnet      : na, "EXP_Magnet",    color = exC_, display = display.data_window)
plot(showEXP ? nearRes     : na, "EXP_ResLevel",  color = exC_, display = display.data_window)
plot(showEXP ? nearSup     : na, "EXP_SupLevel",  color = exC_, display = display.data_window)
plot(showEXP ? pctProfit   : na, "EXP_PctProfit", color = exC_, display = display.data_window)
plot(showEXP ? (bull ? 1 : bear ? -1 : 0) : na, "EXP_Signal", color = exC_, display = display.data_window)
plot(showEXP ? oosEdge     : na, "EXP_EdgeOOS",   color = exC_, display = display.data_window)
plot(showEXP ? effN        : na, "EXP_EffN",      color = exC_, display = display.data_window)
